hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19188","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Damra ibn Thalaba, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two suits of Yemeni suits. So he said: O Damra, do you see these two garments of yours admitting you into Paradise? So he said: If you seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah, I shall not sit until I remove them from me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive Damra ibn Thalaba. So he went quickly until he removed them from him."
